00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:18,820
than the engineers at NASA.

587
00:33:20,860 --> 00:33:23,800
Mission after mission, they face the challenge

588
00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:26,040
of sending spacecraft millions of miles

589
00:33:26,140 --> 00:33:29,280
to the smallest of targets at the farthest reaches

590
00:33:29,380 --> 00:33:30,280
of our solar system.

591
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:34,580
Main engine, so many.

592
00:33:34,581 --> 00:33:43,080
2, 1, 0, and liftoff of the Delta II rocket with Phoenix.

593
00:33:43,180 --> 00:33:47,220
On August 4, 2007, with the launch of NASA's Phoenix Mars

594
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:50,120
lander, they took on one of their most daunting tests

595
00:33:50,220 --> 00:33:51,340
of precision navigation.

596
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:56,740
T plus 130 seconds.

